.TH CCOL_LOG_ALERT 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clog_alert \- emit a log line at ALERT level with a backtrace
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clogger.h>

clog_alert(clog lg, const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Writes a log line at CLOG_ALERT level, capturing __FILE__, __LINE__
and __func__ by itself.  After the structured log line it appends a
stack backtrace, in the same way as clog_error():

  ts=... level=ALERT src=file.c:42 func=handle msg="disk full"
  \et#0 ./myapp(handle+0x1a) [0x7f...]
  \et#1 ./myapp(main+0x42) [0x7f...]

ALERT maps to RFC 5424 syslog severity 1, which reads "alert; action
must be taken immediately".  In CLOG_FMT_SYSLOG mode the library writes
each backtrace frame as a separate syslog message with the same PRI,
TIMESTAMP and MSGID as the original record.

In the order of clog_level_t, ALERT sits between ERROR (severity 3) and
FATAL (severity 0).  Use it for a condition that needs the attention of
an operator at once but need not stop the process.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
lg     Logger handle (clog).
fmt    printf-style format string.
\&...    Format arguments (optional).
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
clog_alert does NOT stop the process, and neither does
clog_error; use clog_fatal when the process must stop.
A backtrace needs the binary to be linked with -rdynamic.  The capture
itself can fail, on a platform with no execinfo.h or on a transient
allocation failure while the library resolves symbol names.  The logger
then writes one "backtrace unavailable" marker line in place of the
usual output for each frame (a marker record in CLOG_FMT_SYSLOG mode),
so the omission is visible instead of silent.
The backtrace write is protected by the shared write lock, so the
backtrace and the preceding log line always appear contiguously.
When memory pressure lasts for a time, or the content of a record
leaves little room before the internal buffer cap, a single backtrace
frame that the library cannot format is omitted, while a shorter frame
that follows it can still go out.  The library never writes an
incomplete frame, so every line that it writes is a complete,
well-formed record.  When not one frame fits, one "backtrace
unavailable" marker line takes their place (a marker record in
CLOG_FMT_SYSLOG mode); this is the same marker that the library uses
when the capture itself fails.  Under such pressure in CLOG_FMT_JSON
mode the library can fail to embed the backtrace at all, and a
"bt_error":"unavailable" key then takes the place of "bt", so the
omission is visible and not silent.
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
clog_alert(lg, "primary database unreachable, failing over");
clog_alert(lg, "disk usage at %d%%, writes may fail soon", pct);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_error (3),
.BR clog_fatal (3),
.BR clog_open_fd_mp (3)
